\f0\fs24 \cf0 Getting Bitwig to recognize the QuNeo MPE :\
\
1. When Bitwig was installed, it automatically created the folder 'Bitwig Studio' within your ~/Documents. Place the controller script (QuNeo MPE.control.js) in\
~/Documents/Bitwig Studio/Controller Scripts/\
\
2. Download and install the QuNeo MPE Application from the Keith McMillen downloads page: https://www.keithmcmillen.com/downloads/\
\
3. If you are on Windows or Linux, you will need to create two virtual MIDI ports (on Windows you will need to google/install loopMIDI): \'93to QuNeo MPE\'94 and \'93from QuNeo MPE\'94.\
\
4. Launch the QuNeo MPE Application and load the QuNeo MPE preset into your QuNeo. Verify that all of the controls work in the visualizer.\
\
5. Open Bitwig and go to the Dashboard (click on the small dots in top middle of the application).\
\
6. Go to the Settings tab (on top).\
\
7. Go to the Controllers tab (on the left).\
\
8. Click on the 'Add' button to the right of 'Controllers'. Select \'91QuNeo MPE\'92 in the 'Keith McMillen' tab.\
(If you are running the QuNeo Application and have the correct virtual MIDI ports enabled, Bitwig gives you a shortcut button to 'Add' the QuNeo MPE controller.\
\
9. The incoming and outgoing MIDI ports will be set to 'None'. Select \'93to QuNeo MPE\'94 as the controller input and \'93from QuNeo MPE\'94 as the contrikker output.\
\
       MIDI from the QuNeo MPE Application should now be coming into Bitwig Studio 8-Track! Try out our synth template to get some sounds going. \
\
\
\
Opening the Keith McMillen MPE synth template :\
\
1. We recommend placing the \'91KMI MPE Bitwig Template' folder in\
~/Documents/Bitwig Studio/Projects\
\
2. Open this folder, and double click the 'KMI MPE Bitwig Template.bwproject' file.\
\
3. Record enable one of the 8 demo synths by clicking the white circle to the right of the synth name, left of the 'S' button. \
\
       Enjoy! If you're not hearing anything, make sure your audio output is correctly selected. These settings are in the Dashboard, under Settings (top row), then Audio (on the left).}